---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Founder's Story" description="Why Belongary exists — 18 years in HR, watching the same cycle repeat.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-plum mb-8">Why This Exists</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-lg">
        I spent 18 years in HR watching the same cycle: engagement surveys nobody acted on, employer branding that hid the truth, and DEI programs that measured everything except whether people actually belonged. The ones who needed honest answers most — the people deciding whether to take the job — never got them.
      </p>

      <p>
        I watched talented people accept offers based on polished careers pages and recruiter promises, only to discover the day-to-day was nothing like the pitch. By the time they knew the truth, they'd already relocated, left a stable job, or burned a bridge. And the next person who came along got the same pitch, because nobody could tell them otherwise.
      </p>

      <p>
        Glassdoor exists, but it answers the wrong question. "Is this a good company?" isn't specific enough. A company can be great for one person and terrible for another. What matters is: <em>would someone like me belong here?</em>
      </p>

      <div class="bg-cream rounded-xl border border-border p-8 my-8">
        <p class="text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-plum mb-3">
          "Would you tell someone like you to take this job?"
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/60">
          That's the question at the heart of every Belongary review. Not "rate your employer." Not "how many stars." Just honest advice from someone who's been there to someone who's deciding.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        I built Belongary because I got tired of watching the cycle repeat. Tired of exit interviews that catalogued problems nobody would fix. Tired of people finding out too late that the culture they were sold wasn't the culture they got.
      </p>

      <p>
        This isn't an employer-branding tool. Companies can't pay to change what's here. They can't remove a review because they don't like it. The only thing that changes their scores is treating people better.
      </p>

      <p>
        If that sounds like a simple idea, it is. Sometimes the most useful things are.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 text-center">
        <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3 bg-coral text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-coral/90 transition-colors shadow-sm">
          Share Your Story
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
